<title>GERMANY: Schmidhuber says no mark devaluation for euro.</title>
<headline>Schmidhuber says no mark devaluation for euro.</headline>
<dateline>BOPPARD, Germany 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Peter Schmidhuber said on Wednesday there was no question of the German mark being devalued when the time came to set the value of the euro.</p>
<p>&quot;There can be no question of a devaluing of the mark when setting the exchange rate level for the euro,&quot; Schmidhuber said in the text of a speech.</p>
<p>European economic and monetary union is due to begin on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
